{
  "name": "How to Plan Your Kitchen Remodel to Avoid Delays",
  "step": [
    {
      "name": "Step 1",
      "text": "Planning is key to a smooth kitchen remodel! Nobody wants unexpected delays. First off, get your design and material selections locked in before any demolition starts. This means picking out your cabinets, countertops, flooring, and even appliances. Believe me, waiting until the last minute for these decisions is a recipe for holdups. Next, make sure you understand the lead times for all your materials. Some custom items can take weeks, or even months, to arrive. HH Remodeling LLC often coordinates sub-trades for plumbing and electrical, so it's essential that these are scheduled in advance to avoid bottlenecks. Also, clarify who’s responsible for securing permits and inspections. If your project involves moving walls or changing plumbing/electrical, permits are likely required. Don't skip this step, as it can cause significant delays and even fines down the road. Keep open communication with your contractor throughout the entire process. Abraham at HH Remodeling LLC emphasizes clear communication, which really helps in keeping things on track. By being proactive and organized, you'll significantly reduce the chances of your kitchen remodel dragging on longer than necessary.",
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "position": 1
    }
  ],
